    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799-a4">

                <pb facs="1284" n="1188" xml:id="pg1188"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    193.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Nubar Pasha to Mr. Beardsley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-04-26"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 26,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Agent and Consul-general</hi>: I have the honor
                    to inclose herewith copy of the letter that Monsieur de Lesseps has addressed to
                    his highness the minister of the interior, by which he informs the Egyptian
                    government that from the 29th of April he will conform to the decision of the
                    Sublime Porte concerning the application of the tariff to ships passing through
                    the canal of Suez.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>NUBAR.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
